zink: placeholder descriptors for devices without robustness2.nullDescriptor (PMB OS)

Since Mesa 24.1 Zink refuses devices without VK_EXT/KHR_robustness2 nullDescriptor. Mali proprietary drivers
(used through Venus on Android) don't have it, so OpenGL was impossible there. Instead of null descriptors,
such devices now get real placeholder resources per context (like Zink did before 24.1 with its dummy
surface / buffer view): a zero-filled 64 KiB buffer (UBO / SSBO / vertex buffer / texel buffers through an
RGBA8 buffer view), a zero-cleared 1x1 RGBA8 texture kept in GENERAL layout (sampled + storage images) and a
nearest/clamp sampler for unbound sampler states. Unbound vertex buffers read with stride 0 where the stride
is dynamic. Features that write null descriptors with no place for a placeholder are disabled on such
devices: descriptor-buffer mode, bindless textures and fbfetch.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c
